From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mscoree: ICorDebug object values, arrays, classes, modules and assemblies over Wine Mono's agent.

A .NET debugger looking into a stopped program got as far as a reference: Dereference of anything but a
string was E_NOTIMPL, and there were no modules, assemblies or classes to find types and fields with.
Now a reference to an object dereferences to an ICorDebugObjectValue whose fields (by metadata token, the
class's or a base class's, static ones too) come from the agent (OBJECT_REF GET_VALUES); a struct comes with
its fields, an enum is also a generic value, IntPtr/UIntPtr are primitives; an array is an
ICorDebugArrayValue (element type, rank, dimensions, base indices, elements). Values with a home (a frame's
local or argument, an object's field, a static field, an array element) can be set
(ICorDebugGenericValue/ReferenceValue::SetValue). EnumerateAppDomains (the one), the domain's assemblies
(APPDOMAIN GET_ASSEMBLIES), an assembly's module, a module's name, metadata (the assembly's image from the
agent read by the metadata engine, also when Wine Mono's loader handed out a mapped image),
GetFunctionFromToken/GetClassFromToken, GetModuleFromMetaDataInterface (by MVID), ICorDebugFunction
GetModule/GetClass, ICorDebugClass GetStaticFieldValue, ICorDebugThread::GetAppDomain.
include/cordebug.idl: ICorDebugArrayValue as declared in dotnet/runtime's cordebug.idl (MIT).
Boxed values arrive unboxed from the agent (as the struct): no ICorDebugBoxValue.
